<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell late-April Bombay naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell late-April Bombay naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) offered to sell by tender 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) for April 21-25 lifting, free-on-board (fob) Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on April 10 and bids are valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN tender for a cargo lifting March 10-12, was awarded at $25.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on an fob basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
